mod_uploader 3.2.0 - altered FreeBSD / Apache 2.4 version

Original software: Tetsuya Kimata.
Upstream: https://github.com/kimata/mod_uploader
Baseline commit: 31632a29138b18b7adbf533416a0ec660f1b07ac

This is an altered source version, not an official upstream release.
It contains FreeBSD/Clang build adjustments, Apache 2.4 request handling
changes, multipart and upload security fixes, regression tests and a
FreeBSD Port candidate. See README.md and docs/FREEBSD-ja.md.

The original copyright and license notices are retained. The modifications
and new source files in this work are distributed under the zlib license
in COPYING. Authors of the original work are not represented as authors
of these modifications. Other existing file-specific notices still apply.

Validation: the user reported that mod_uploader worked on their FreeBSD /
Apache setup after the catch-handler correction. Exact system versions
and individual feature results were not supplied. Local C++ regression
tests use Windows/G++ and simulated APR/httpd APIs; they do not certify
FreeBSD Ports packaging or complete HTTP functionality.

Security update: version-4 hashed password metadata, offline verified backups,
storage exclusion, and expiring session-bound signed CSRF tokens.
See docs/SECURITY-MIGRATION-ja.md before replacing an existing installation.

Port revision 4: require Apache-authenticated administration; bound per-IP password attempts and cross-process concurrent hashing; make Locker cleanup non-throwing with error reporting. See SECURITY-MIGRATION-ja.md.

Port revision 5: audit fixes validate before eviction, serialize capacity changes, reject malformed text/metadata and unsafe lock takeover, close mail/thumbnail authorization gaps, handle missing payloads and cleanup failures, and escape error/redirect output.
The audit also fixes generation checks, concurrent identifiers, shared-state alignment and synchronization, and configuration-pool lifetime across Apache DSO unloading.

Port revision 6: support root and subpath VirtualHost mounts with validated URI routing, normalize BaseUrl once, and provide canonical static URLs and explicit static-handler examples. Password format, authentication, upload limits and thumbnail implementation are retained.
Correct the FreeBSD -L flag spelling for direct libtool builds, including ImageMagick-enabled configurations.

Port revision 7: verified offline backup/restore, conservative journal recovery,
capacity/dependency checks, reversible upload eviction with durable staging,
bounded raster-only thumbnails, explicit error statuses and reduced compiler warnings.
Metadata remains version 4. See docs/OPERATIONS-ja.md and OPERATIONS-VALIDATION-ja.md.

Port revision 8: declare the patch-phase Perl dependency and the FreeBSD
pkg-config search path for ImageMagick 7 thumbnail builds. Module source,
templates and storage format are unchanged from revision 7.
